{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2119,"code_snippet":"_estimated = estimate_tokens(messages)\nif _estimated > _input_threshold:","reasoning_trace":"Traced the input estimate through cmd_invoke: the pre-flight replaces _preflight_estimated/_walk_estimate with the provider count_tokens answer (cheval.py:1841-1842 via ceiling.gate :409-412), the per-hop I1 fit at :2090 consumes _walk_estimate, but the walk gate at :2119 re-runs the chars/3.5 heuristic and compares it against the same bound. Two numbers for one input.","finding":"Walk gate discards the authoritative count_tokens estimate; a request the pre-flight dispatched is refused ROUTING_MISS on every HTTP hop when the heuristic over-counts (prose: ~4 chars/token vs 3.5).","critique":"D-1.4 says the provider count replaces the estimate near the bound; the walk gate silently undoes it and the count round-trip is paid for nothing. The chain falls to the CLI hop or exhausts.","remediation":"At :2119 use `_estimated = _walk_estimate if _walk_estimate is not None else estimate_tokens(messages)` (and in the message_redacted text); add an e2e row with heuristic > bound >= count asserting one dispatch and no ROUTING_MISS.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-697","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"configuration","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/resources/config.ts","line":172,"code_snippet":"model: \"opus\",","reasoning_trace":"getTokenBudget keys GENERATED_TOKEN_BUDGETS (truncation.generated.ts:19-52) and the hand table by the raw model string; grep finds no GENERATED_MODEL_ALIASES or any alias table anywhere under pr/head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/ (resources or dist). The later workspace snapshot adds exactly that export and a budgetId() alias step, corroborating the gap at this head.","finding":"Default model `opus` (and personas quick.md:2 `tiny`, security.md:2 `opus`) is an alias the Bridgebuilder budget table cannot resolve; the default review sizes from TOKEN_BUDGETS[\"default\"] (100K/4096) instead of the 160K/32K catalog row the old concrete default resolved to. DEFAULTS.maxInputTokens 200_000 (:176) also exceeds the 180K probed bound.","critique":"The PR's stated invariant is that every size decision derives from the resolved catalog entry; the Bridgebuilder default now derives from the fallback row. The PR's tests only probe concrete ids so nothing fails.","remediation":"Emit the yaml aliases block into truncation.generated.ts and resolve it in getTokenBudget before the lookup (or keep a concrete default); add a test that getTokenBudget('opus') equals getTokenBudget('claude-opus-5'); clamp maxInputTokens to the generated row.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1188","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1188.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":1843,"code_snippet":"_ceiling_unverified = _preflight_outcome.unverified","reasoning_trace":"_ceiling_unverified is assigned once from the head entry's GateOutcome and read unchanged at :2256 (error class) and :2297 (429 short-circuit) inside the per-entry chain loop; no per-hop recomputation exists.","finding":"The head entry's unverified status is applied to every fallback hop, so a calibrated fallback's ordinary 429 exits RATE_LIMITED with a calibration record written for an entry that was never unverified, and the converse mis-classes a provider verdict.","critique":"Per-hop bound decisions already exist in _lookup_max_input_tokens; the status should come from that hop's CeilingDecision.","remediation":"Recompute `unverified = policy == 'derived' and not decision.calibrated and estimate > decision.probed` per hop; keep the head's flag for the envelope only.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-697","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2297,"code_snippet":"except RateLimitError as _e:\n    if _ceiling_unverified:\n        return _calibration_needed_exit(... error_class=\"RATE_LIMIT_UNVERIFIED\" ...)","reasoning_trace":"RateLimitError at head (types.py:225-229) carries only provider and retry_after; anthropic_adapter.py:343 raises it without the 429 body. The arm fires on any RateLimitError while the flag is set.","finding":"Any 429 while dispatching above the probed bound ends the call and writes a RATE_LIMIT_UNVERIFIED row, although the comment scopes it to the token-limit class; a plain requests-per-minute 429 never reaches the declared fallback.","critique":"Opt-in only (LOA_CHEVAL_UNCALIBRATED_CEILING=derived) and conservative, hence medium.","remediation":"Parse the 429 body for the tokens-per-minute shape into a token_limited flag on RateLimitError and gate the short-circuit on it; otherwise fall through to the PROVIDER_OUTAGE walk.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-754","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/retry.py","line":495,"code_snippet":"request = replace(request, max_tokens=room)\ncontinue","reasoning_trace":"The shrink `continue`s inside `for attempt in range(max_retries + 1)` without setting last_typed_error; on the final iteration the loop exits and :527-532 raises RetriesExhaustedError with no typed cause; cheval.py:2338 classes it FALLBACK_EXHAUSTED and walks. test_ceiling_retry.py uses max_retries 3 only.","finding":"When the provider context-limit error arrives on the last retry slot (max_retries 0, or after transient failures), the shrunk request is never sent, the typed error is lost, and the oversized payload walks to the next voice — the outcome D-1.1b forbids — with no observed-bound row.","critique":"The single shrink should not consume an ordinary retry slot.","remediation":"Give the shrink its own attempt outside the retry count (or raise instead of continue when attempt == max_retries) and set last_typed_error = e; add a max_retries 0 test.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-755","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/755.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/metering/pricing.py","line":168,"code_snippet":"if threshold is not None and input_tokens > threshold:","reasoning_trace":"ledger.py:162-166 passes input_tokens and the cache token counts as separate arguments; anthropic_adapter.py:557-562 maps usage.input_tokens (which excludes cache_read/cache_creation) and the cache fields separately. The threshold tests input_tokens alone while the multipliers at :171-172 scale cr_cost/cw_cost.","finding":"The long-context premium threshold ignores cache tokens: a 60K fresh + 180K cached request is billed at base rates and `long_context` is not set, so cost-report long_context_rows and the daily budget enforcer under-count.","critique":"Cache traffic is treated as input for the multiplier but not for the threshold.","remediation":"Test `input_tokens + cache_read_tokens + cache_creation_tokens > threshold`; document in the catalog which total the threshold applies to.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-1023","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1023.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2005,"code_snippet":"_obs = int(observed) if isinstance(observed, int) and observed > 0 else int(_walk_estimate or 0)\n_ceiling_record_observed(... observed_input_tokens=_obs, ... provider_limit=provider_limit)","reasoning_trace":"anthropic_adapter.py:361/503 types any 400/413 whose body matches is_context_limit_message (ceiling.py:157-175) and fills input_tokens/limit from parse_context_limit of the free-text body. _calibration_needed_exit persists those numbers (or the heuristic estimate when none are stated) via record_observed; observed_for (ceiling.py:249-260) takes min(observed, limit+1) and input_bound (:122-123) lowers the bound to observed-1 with no floor, no upper bound, no consistency check, no expiry.","finding":"Numbers parsed from a provider error body become a persistent input bound for the (provider, model) until an operator runs the paid probe; a single malformed or hostile message of the shape 'prompt is too long: 1 tokens > 1 maximum' (or a 413 byte-size refusal on a text-light payload) sets the bound near zero and every later request preempts with CONTEXT_TOO_LARGE.","critique":"Data from the network is trusted as a bound without plausibility checks; the 429 path already records without lowering, so a fallback exists.","remediation":"Before lowering: require FLOOR_MAX_TOKENS <= limit <= context_window, observed >= cheval's own estimate, and input_tokens > limit for the parsed shape; record with observed_input_tokens null (no bound effect) when the message states nothing; consider an expiry on observed rows.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-1284","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1284.html","CWE-20","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"DEV-001","category":"devops","criterion":"resource_limits","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/flatline-orchestrator.sh","line":1027,"code_snippet":"per_call_max_tokens=\"$(flatline_voice_max_tokens \"$model_override\")\"","reasoning_trace":"FLATLINE_VOICE_MAX_TOKENS_CAP=64000 (:129) applies to review, skeptic and score calls on every 128K-declared entry; DEFAULT_MODEL_TIMEOUT=120 (:115) is passed by run_phase1/run_inquiry. The removed cycle-124 comment kept 16000 so the per-call timeout never met a 64K generation; tests/unit/cycle-124-dispatch-budgets.bats:5-8 still states that rationale.","finding":"Every Flatline voice call now carries a 64K output budget under a 120 s timeout; the scorer emits a small JSON array, so the cap mostly lengthens a runaway generation into the timeout.","critique":"Speculative, low confidence: the hazard partly pre-dated the PR (16K at 50 tok/s already exceeds 120 s).","remediation":"Let the mode supply a cap (score <= 16K) over the catalog budget, or scale the phase timeout; fix the bats header.","confidence":"low","references":["CWE-400","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":82,"code_snippet":"_BETA_HEADER_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*-\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$\")","reasoning_trace":"Executed: re.match with this pattern accepts 'context-1m-2025-08-07\\n' (True); fullmatch rejects it. The value is joined into the anthropic-beta header at :174-181. httpx/urllib refuse header values with newlines, so the outcome is an opaque transport exception rather than injection.","finding":"The beta-header allowlist is weaker than documented: a trailing newline passes re.match and the ConfigError the code promises becomes a transport failure.","critique":"Catalog-sourced, so low; the allowlist is the stated defence (CWE-113 class) and should be exact.","remediation":"Use _BETA_HEADER_RE.fullmatch(item) or end the pattern with \\Z.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-113","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/113.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/metering/pricing.py","line":290,"code_snippet":"def _mult(value): ... return m if m > 0 else 1.0","reasoning_trace":"Executed _long_context_fields({'threshold_tokens':200000,'input_multiplier':float('inf')}) -> multiplier inf; PyYAML parses `.inf`. calculate_total_cost then does int(inp_cost * inf) -> OverflowError after the billed call, inside create_ledger_entry.","finding":"A non-finite or absurd multiplier passes parsing and raises (or inflates cost without bound) after the provider call, so the completed call's cost is never recorded.","critique":"The threshold is validated; the multipliers are not.","remediation":"Require math.isfinite(m) and clamp to a sane range (e.g. 1.0..10.0), else treat as no premium tier.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-682","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/682.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"logging","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2022,"code_snippet":"\"message_redacted\": str(_exc),","reasoning_trace":"cheval.py at head imports no redaction helper; the models_failed row and the stderr _error_json line carry str(_exc) verbatim (the provider 400 body). Every other models_failed arm in cmd_invoke does the same (:2155, :2243, :2268, :2285, :2311, :2327, :2349); the envelope path is redacted field-level by the untouched loa_cheval/audit/modelinv.py (redact_payload_strings). The dissent's cited test does not exist at head.","finding":"The provider's raw error text lands unredacted in the stderr error JSON and is only redacted at envelope emit; same class as the existing arms, not introduced here, but the new field name promises redaction the record path does not do.","critique":"Anthropic context-limit bodies are fixed-shape and do not echo the prompt; a proxy could.","remediation":"Run str(_exc) through redaction.redact_exception before recording and before the stderr line; keep only the class and parsed numbers on stderr.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-532","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/532.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-007","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/routing/ceiling.py","line":157,"code_snippet":"_CONTEXT_LIMIT_MARKERS = (... \"context length\", \"context window\", ... \"input length\", ...)","reasoning_trace":"is_context_limit_message is a substring test over the body; any Anthropic 400 mentioning the context window for another reason is typed ProviderContextLimitError, never walked, and (via SEC-001) lowers the observed bound.","finding":"The context-limit classifier is broad; non-size 400s containing these words are treated as the provider's size verdict.","critique":"Anchor on the two known message shapes plus request_too_large.","remediation":"Classify on _RE_INPUT_ONLY / _RE_INPUT_PLUS_OUTPUT matches and the 413 request_too_large code; keep the marker list as a logged hint only.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-697","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-008","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/base.py","line":1000,"code_snippet":"import tiktoken  # noqa: F401\nmethod = \"tiktoken\"","reasoning_trace":"estimate_input sets method from the import succeeding, while estimate_tokens (:928-937) may still fall back to chars/3.5 when the encoding fetch fails offline; the envelope's estimator.method misattributes the number.","finding":"`method: tiktoken` is reported whenever the module imports, regardless of which path produced the count.","critique":"The method should come from the function that computed the estimate.","remediation":"Return (tokens, method) from estimate_tokens and use it.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-684","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/684.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-009","category":"code_quality","criterion":"tests","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/tests/test_ceiling_probe_write_catalog.py","line":66,"code_snippet":"... if False else tool.write_catalog(\"      claude-opus-5:\\n        context_window: 1\\n\", ...)","reasoning_trace":"The third pytest.raises block is a conditional expression whose first branch is unreachable (`if False`).","finding":"Dead branch obscures the assertion's intent (a block missing effective_input_ceiling).","critique":"Keep only the live call.","remediation":"Replace the expression with the minimal-fixture write_catalog call alone.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-561","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/561.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-010","category":"code_quality","criterion":"resource_cleanup","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":173,"code_snippet":"fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(...)\nwith os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", ...) as fh: fh.write(new)\nos.replace(tmp, path)","reasoning_trace":"Compared with ceiling.record_observed (:294-305) which unlinks the temp file on failure; _write_catalog_file has no try/except around the write and replace.","finding":"A failed catalog write leaves `.model-config.*.tmp` beside the catalog under .claude/defaults/.","critique":"Mirror the adapter-side writer.","remediation":"Wrap write + replace in try/except BaseException with os.unlink(tmp) before re-raising.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-459","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/459.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"timeouts","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/base.py","line":171,"code_snippet":"_NON_ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OUTPUT_CAP = 16_000","reasoning_trace":"default_max_tokens now returns up to 16K for OpenAI/Google/Bedrock hops while only the Anthropic adapter scales its non-streaming read timeout with max_tokens; the comment two lines above says such fixture moves 'must move deliberately'.","finding":"Non-Anthropic default output rises 4096 -> 16000 against a fixed read timeout on the legacy transport; a long legitimate generation becomes a 504 and a billed retry.","critique":"Speculative, low confidence.","remediation":"Scale the OpenAI/Google non-streaming read timeout with max_tokens as the Anthropic adapter does, or keep 4096 on the legacy transport.","confidence":"low","references":["CWE-400","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"]}
