{"id":"DEV-001","category":"devops","criterion":"resource_limits","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/flatline-orchestrator.sh","line":1027,"code_snippet":"per_call_max_tokens=\"$(flatline_voice_max_tokens \"$model_override\")\"","reasoning_trace":"FLATLINE_VOICE_MAX_TOKENS_CAP=64000 (:129) applies to review, skeptic and score calls on every 128K-declared entry; DEFAULT_MODEL_TIMEOUT=120 (:115) is passed by run_phase1/run_inquiry. The removed cycle-124 comment kept 16000 so the per-call timeout never met a 64K generation; tests/unit/cycle-124-dispatch-budgets.bats:5-8 still states that rationale.","finding":"Every Flatline voice call now carries a 64K output budget under a 120 s timeout; the scorer emits a small JSON array, so the cap mostly lengthens a runaway generation into the timeout.","critique":"Speculative, low confidence: the hazard partly pre-dated the PR (16K at 50 tok/s already exceeds 120 s).","remediation":"Let the mode supply a cap (score <= 16K) over the catalog budget, or scale the phase timeout; fix the bats header.","confidence":"low","references":["CWE-400","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/anthropic_adapter.py","line":82,"code_snippet":"_BETA_HEADER_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*-\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$\")","reasoning_trace":"Executed: re.match with this pattern accepts 'context-1m-2025-08-07\\n' (True); fullmatch rejects it. The value is joined into the anthropic-beta header at :174-181. httpx/urllib refuse header values with newlines, so the outcome is an opaque transport exception rather than injection.","finding":"The beta-header allowlist is weaker than documented: a trailing newline passes re.match and the ConfigError the code promises becomes a transport failure.","critique":"Catalog-sourced, so low; the allowlist is the stated defence (CWE-113 class) and should be exact.","remediation":"Use _BETA_HEADER_RE.fullmatch(item) or end the pattern with \\Z.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-113","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/113.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/metering/pricing.py","line":290,"code_snippet":"def _mult(value): ... return m if m > 0 else 1.0","reasoning_trace":"Executed _long_context_fields({'threshold_tokens':200000,'input_multiplier':float('inf')}) -> multiplier inf; PyYAML parses `.inf`. calculate_total_cost then does int(inp_cost * inf) -> OverflowError after the billed call, inside create_ledger_entry.","finding":"A non-finite or absurd multiplier passes parsing and raises (or inflates cost without bound) after the provider call, so the completed call's cost is never recorded.","critique":"The threshold is validated; the multipliers are not.","remediation":"Require math.isfinite(m) and clamp to a sane range (e.g. 1.0..10.0), else treat as no premium tier.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-682","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/682.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"logging","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2022,"code_snippet":"\"message_redacted\": str(_exc),","reasoning_trace":"cheval.py at head imports no redaction helper; the models_failed row and the stderr _error_json line carry str(_exc) verbatim (the provider 400 body). Every other models_failed arm in cmd_invoke does the same (:2155, :2243, :2268, :2285, :2311, :2327, :2349); the envelope path is redacted field-level by the untouched loa_cheval/audit/modelinv.py (redact_payload_strings). The dissent's cited test does not exist at head.","finding":"The provider's raw error text lands unredacted in the stderr error JSON and is only redacted at envelope emit; same class as the existing arms, not introduced here, but the new field name promises redaction the record path does not do.","critique":"Anthropic context-limit bodies are fixed-shape and do not echo the prompt; a proxy could.","remediation":"Run str(_exc) through redaction.redact_exception before recording and before the stderr line; keep only the class and parsed numbers on stderr.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-532","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/532.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-007","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/routing/ceiling.py","line":157,"code_snippet":"_CONTEXT_LIMIT_MARKERS = (... \"context length\", \"context window\", ... \"input length\", ...)","reasoning_trace":"is_context_limit_message is a substring test over the body; any Anthropic 400 mentioning the context window for another reason is typed ProviderContextLimitError, never walked, and (via SEC-001) lowers the observed bound.","finding":"The context-limit classifier is broad; non-size 400s containing these words are treated as the provider's size verdict.","critique":"Anchor on the two known message shapes plus request_too_large.","remediation":"Classify on _RE_INPUT_ONLY / _RE_INPUT_PLUS_OUTPUT matches and the 413 request_too_large code; keep the marker list as a logged hint only.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-697","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/697.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-008","category":"code_quality","criterion":"correctness","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/base.py","line":1000,"code_snippet":"import tiktoken  # noqa: F401\nmethod = \"tiktoken\"","reasoning_trace":"estimate_input sets method from the import succeeding, while estimate_tokens (:928-937) may still fall back to chars/3.5 when the encoding fetch fails offline; the envelope's estimator.method misattributes the number.","finding":"`method: tiktoken` is reported whenever the module imports, regardless of which path produced the count.","critique":"The method should come from the function that computed the estimate.","remediation":"Return (tokens, method) from estimate_tokens and use it.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-684","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/684.html"]}
